5.3. Improving Abiotic Stress Tolerance in Plants
Nitrogen acquisition and uptake can be restricted under abiotic stress conditions, such as drought and salinity. External fluctuations of N supply to plants caused by abiotic stress occurrence have been shown to hinder NO3 acquisition as well as other subsequent events due to water scarcity [153]. As per some evidence, high- and low-affinity NO3 transporters and glutamate synthase-encoding genes [154], and phytohormones biosynthetic and signaling pathway genes [155,156] (in addition to well-characterized abscisic


